# Article ↔ calculator call-out

When an article and a live calculator answer the same reader question, each page gets the shared high-contrast call-out pointing at the other.

## Article → calculator

The last sentence of the copy must be followed by the call-out — before FAQ, newsletter, related reading, disclaimer, and footer.

- Add `calculatorCallout` to both `assets/i18n/en/articles/{slug}.json` and the FR file:
  `{ "href": "/calculators/{live-slug}/", "calculatorName": "Exact calculator title" }`
- Use one primary calculator. Secondary tools stay in related reading.
- Default copy lives in `common.calculatorCallout`.

## Calculator → article

After the tool and any remaining explanation — before related links, FAQ, or the disclaimer.

- Add the calculator slug to `CALCULATOR_PRIMARY_ARTICLE` in `build/lib/article-calc-callout.js`.
- Use one primary article: the piece that answers the calculator’s actual question. Other matching articles stay in related reading.
- The build injects `.calc-article-callout` from that map. Do not hand-build a second CTA card.
- Default copy lives in `common.articleCallout`.
- Do not point a live calculator at an unpublished article.

## Do

- Verify the href exists and does not overclaim what the tool or article covers. If it omits a rule the other page taught, add `note`.
- When shipping a new pair, add both directions in the same change.

## Do not

- Do not add a call-out when no live counterpart applies the page’s actual question.
- Do not invent a calculator or article, link a draft, or point at a generic nearby page to fill the slot.
- Do not place the call-out inside FAQ, related reading, or the footer.

## Copy

Override `heading`, `lead` (`{name}`), or `note` only when the default would mislead.
